From: Joel Winarske <joel.winarske@linux.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Forward HOME and the policy escape hatch to sub-builds

The nested CMake invocations start from an empty environment (`env -i`) with
only PATH preserved, so nothing the outer build was configured with reaches
them. Two things have to.

HOME: download_external_sources() forwards only PATH, while
build_external_dependencies() a hundred lines below already forwards HOME as
well -- the two disagree about what a sub-build needs. On macOS the download
step reaches CocoaPods, which invokes brew, which refuses to run without a home
directory:

    Error: $HOME must be set to run brew.

CMAKE_POLICY_VERSION_MINIMUM: CMake 4 removed compatibility with
cmake_minimum_required(VERSION < 3.5), and several pinned dependencies still
declare one -- Firestore's own tree fails at cmake_policy() before anything is
compiled. Passing the escape hatch through the environment is what makes it
reach them: it initializes the cache of every new build tree however deeply
nested, so one variable covers dependencies this file never names. It expands to
nothing when the outer build did not set it.

Linux gets both through its own rewrite of this environment setup; this is the
same fix expressed against the unmodified upstream file.

--- a/cmake/external_rules.cmake
+++ b/cmake/external_rules.cmake
@@ -26,7 +26,11 @@ function(download_external_sources)
     set(ENV_COMMAND "")
   else()
     set(firebase_command_line_path "$ENV{PATH}")
-    set(ENV_COMMAND env -i PATH=${firebase_command_line_path})
+    set(firebase_command_line_home "$ENV{HOME}")
+    set(ENV_COMMAND env -i PATH=${firebase_command_line_path} HOME=${firebase_command_line_home})
+    if(CMAKE_POLICY_VERSION_MINIMUM)
+      list(APPEND ENV_COMMAND "CMAKE_POLICY_VERSION_MINIMUM=${CMAKE_POLICY_VERSION_MINIMUM}")
+    endif()
   endif()
 
   if(IOS)
@@ -142,6 +146,9 @@ function(build_external_dependencies)
     set(firebase_command_line_path "$ENV{PATH}")
     set(firebase_command_line_home "$ENV{HOME}")
     set(ENV_COMMAND env -i PATH=${firebase_command_line_path} HOME=${firebase_command_line_home} )
+    if(CMAKE_POLICY_VERSION_MINIMUM)
+      list(APPEND ENV_COMMAND "CMAKE_POLICY_VERSION_MINIMUM=${CMAKE_POLICY_VERSION_MINIMUM}")
+    endif()
   endif()
 
   message(STATUS "CMake generator: ${CMAKE_GENERATOR}")
